            "The analyst can account for confounds through regression-based approaches that include multiple predictors in the same model, often called meta-regression, and should consider always controlling for methods confounders such as study design and effect size computation details that are not central to the substantive research questions but could contaminate the results of interest.",
            "Moderator analyses are often underpowered, especially for small numbers of studies, and when conducting a large number of moderator tests the analyst could find a stray significant moderator and herald that result as a main finding when that result might just be due to chance.",
